          <Pad Id="LOM6NeKR1UDLCRmif1dOqL" Bounds="1018,22,376,525" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="THE CONFIGURATION FILE&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;If you own a genuine AxiDraw pen plotter, you won’t need to make many changes to the configuration file. However, you do need to specify which model you’re using (A4 or A3) and adjust the corresponding settings accordingly.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;If you’re using a pen plotter from IDraw, a few additional adjustments are required:&#xD;&#xA;•Stepsize Difference&#xD;&#xA;The IDraw plotter has a smaller stepsize compared to the AxiDraw. As a result, you need to scale your drawing down by 25% before exporting the .svg. This scaling must be done in the software you use to create the file — it is not handled automatically.&#xD;&#xA;•Maximum Plot Area&#xD;&#xA;You’ll need to adjust the maximum plot dimensions in the configuration file. For example, if you're using an IDraw A3, increase the A3 dimensions by 25% and convert them to inches. Then replace one of the existing plot size presets with these new values.&#xD;&#xA;•Pen-Up / Pen-Down Reversed&#xD;&#xA;For some reason, the IDraw plotter uses reversed logic for pen states. The values for “PenUp” and “PenDown” must be swapped.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="NNfL31lndhhP82QUX7fl1L" Bounds="1438,21,501,152" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="LOOKING UNDER THE HOOD&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;This patch relies heavily on the Executor node to send commands to the plotter. Depending on how Python and the AxiDraw CLI are installed on your system, the setup works in two different ways:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;If AxiDraw CLI is installed globally, you can call the axicli command directly from the Executor node.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="AxJxrfrnskDMmuCZCZNOnj" Bounds="1447,454,484,38" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="(... and this is the safe way we are using)">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
